        },
        "texto": "See also Mark 6:23. It is common for public dancers at festivals in great houses to ask for rewards from the company. An instance is recorded by Thevenot, in his Travels in Persia, which reminds us of this extravagant promise of Herod. Shah Abbas was on one occasion so pleased wi…"
      },
      "c-c19428059de7683e": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-671",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "See also Mark 6:43; Luke 9:17; John 6:13. The baskets now used in the East resemble very much those which are represented on the monuments of Egypt. They are often like our own in shape, material, and workmanship. The baskets here referred to (κόφινοι) were probably the ordinary…"
      },
      "c-dfd5c00b38c1bd6a": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-670",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "See also Mark 6:41; Luke 9:16; John 6:11. It was customary among the Jews to give thanks to God at the commencement of every meal. The usual form was, “Blessed be thou, O Lord our God the king of the world, who produced bread out of the earth.” They also had a form of blessing fo…"
      }
